    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="2d13cc7b-56fb-5a25-bffc-8d3445fd07ff" activityNameId="329cc482-7c4c-5315-9935-f945e5eee00a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Door leaf, outer, wood-glass, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Door leaf, outer, wood-glass, at plant
The measures of the visible door leaf are 1m x 2m. The size of the glass insert for the door leaf is 0.74m2. 1m2 of visible glass-wood door leaf weighs 40.5kg. The bill of materials is based on data from door manufactures.;
UUID: 7d6338e2-8674-3387-b6ce-234458b4cfdb
Included are the materials used in an outer glass-wood door leaf (without surface treatment). Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: Data apply to the supply in Switzerland.
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 door manufactures in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7d6338e2-8674-3387-b6ce-234458b4cfdb.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
